WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.769
Additional BIND servers in AWS align with
the workbook's DNS design when they are

2
00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:09.696
forwarders or resolvers
under central configuration,

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:12.513
logged to the SOC,
owned and with a reason.

4
00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:17.350
BIND aligns when it's a resolver or
forwarder whose configuration comes from

5
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.112
the policy plane: its forwarding, its
addresses and its logging all governed.

6
00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:26.238
It aligns as a deliberate bridge,
with an owner and an end date.

7
00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:30.475
It aligns when Git configures it, and
when it's hardened and inventoried.

8
00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:35.415
It creates a silo when it hosts zones
authored apart from the DDI platform,

9
00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:40.435
when it's edited by hand, when it skips
the shared Protective DNS, validation

10
00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:45.600
and logging, or when it duplicates the
Route 53 Resolver for no stated reason.
